5,1,1,talk,Kenji,,We need to make sure the new system actually works in the yards. I'm worried about the equipment and the peak season rush.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree we need stability, but we must also look at the long-term financial impact. Headline prices often hide the true cost of ownership.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"We should focus on why previous projects failed. Specifically, I want to see who was actually responsible when things broke and how the scope shifted.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Rin,,"I don't want a system that just gets old and dusty! Or one where we pay people to fix it, but it stays broken. Let's look at the history!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Servas,,It is the people who carry the weight of any system. I wish to understand the burden on our staff and the reality of our training capacity.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, money is important, but if the depot stops moving during a cutover, we lose more than just the budget.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"True, but a system that bankrupts us through hidden renewal fees is a different kind of failure. We need to see the actual invoices.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the cutover failure is usually a symptom of poor ownership. I'll look into the outage support to see where the accountability gap lies.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that sounds like a mystery! I want to know if the tools we use just keep getting patched up forever without actually getting better.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Servas,,"Patience, my friends. Let us remember that a tool is only as good as the hand that wields it. We must see if our people are stretched too thin.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I'll check the yard devices and the peak-season cutover. We can't afford a crash when the freight is piling up.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,I will examine the renewal invoices and the board minutes. I want to see how the approved budget compares to the actual spending over time.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Asuka,,I will investigate the support ownership during last winter's outage and the warehouse rule changes after new accounts.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Rin,,I'm going to look at the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift from 2018! I bet there are some messy secrets there.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Servas,,I shall look into the administrator retirements and the depot supervisors' experience with the last rollout. The human element is our true foundation.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
