35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"It's worse than I thought. Our yard gear is a mess, and trying to switch systems during peak season is a disaster waiting to happen.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings confirm my fears. The board ignores operating costs, and modular licenses are bleeding us dry through annual increases. We need a fixed-cost model.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"We have a systemic problem. Last winter, no one took ownership of the outage. Furthermore, our ""frozen"" requirements are ignored the moment a new account is signed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found it! The dispatch tool is like a dinosaur that we're too scared to update, and the 2018 data move was a total mess that we just lived with!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My heart grows heavy. We are losing our institutional memory to retirement, and our crews are ignoring training because it doesn't fit their reality.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if no one took ownership last time, we need a vendor who will actually be on-site at the depots, not just in a remote office.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, on-site support is great, but if it's billed as an ""additional service"" every month, it's just another hidden cost. We need a flat fee.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, a flat fee is useless if the vendor claims the request is ""out of scope"" because the business changed. We need a flexible but accountable governance model.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Why do we keep paying people to do things that stay broken? If the 2018 move was a mess, we can't let the new vendor just ""lift and shift"" our bad data!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right. But remember, the data is moved by people. If those people are exhausted and unsupported, the data will always be messy.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I don't care about the data as much as the hardware. If the new system requires the latest tablets, we're doomed. It has to work on what we have.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm seeing a pattern. We've been tricked by ""low entry costs"" before. I will vote against any candidate that uses a modular, pay-as-you-go pricing structure.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I will prioritize the candidate that offers a single point of contact for support. I cannot accept another winter where we spend two days arguing about who is responsible.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I want the one that actually cleans up the old stuff! No more ""quietly aging"" systems. We need a fresh start, not a fancy coat of paint on a rusty car.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"I am concerned for the supervisors. If the vendor just sends a manual and a one-day webinar, the system will fail. We need hands-on, empathetic guidance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
