60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Anchor is the only one that sounds like they'll actually be here in the yards. Having an engineering team on-site is exactly what we need for the hardware.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Anchor's on-premise model is the most predictable. No monthly subscription creep or modular license hikes. It's a capital expense we can control.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Meridian's ""fixed configuration process"" sounds risky given how our business changes, but their regional service team might provide the single point of accountability we lack.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Tessera sounds too fancy! ""Application marketplace"" just sounds like more things that will age in place. Anchor feels like they'll actually fix the foundation.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"I see the wisdom in Anchor. Their presence on-site is not just for the machines, but for the people. It provides the human support our tired staff deserves.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, Meridian's regional team is still remote. If a scanner dies in the yard during peak, a regional team doesn't help. Anchor's engineers do.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, I strongly advise against Corvus. Modular licensing is exactly how we've been bled dry in the past. It's a financial trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, you're right about the physical presence. However, I'm worried Anchor's ""built for transport"" means it's rigid. But accountability is my priority. Anchor's on-site team is a clear owner.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If Anchor is on-site, they can't just leave a mess like the 2018 data move! They have to stay until it actually works. I like that!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"When we are thin on people, we cannot ask them to learn a complex cloud suite from a partner firm. We need the vendor to walk beside them.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm sold on Anchor. They are the only ones who seem to understand that the depot floor is where the real work happens.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. Anchor's model avoids the recurring operating cost traps that the board ignores. It's the most fiscally responsible choice for the long term.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I've weighed the risk of rigidity against the risk of fragmented accountability. The lack of ownership last winter was a critical failure. Anchor's on-site presence solves this.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Anchor! Let's get rid of the dinosaur systems and the messy patches. Let's have someone actually fix it for real!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,It is a gentle path to choose the one who offers their presence. Our people are the heart of this company; Anchor is the only choice that protects that heart.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
